<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<paragraphs xml:id="para-pretext-structure" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Document Structure</title>

  <p>
    PreTeXt documents follow a strict hierarchical organization: <c>&lt;pretext&gt;</c> contains <c>&lt;docinfo&gt;</c>
    and <c>&lt;book&gt;</c> (or <c>&lt;article&gt;</c>), which hierarchically nests <c>&lt;part&gt;</c>,
    <c>&lt;chapter&gt;</c>, <c>&lt;section&gt;</c>, <c>&lt;subsection&gt;</c>, and division blocks like
    <c>&lt;introduction&gt;</c>, <c>&lt;paragraphs&gt;</c>, and <c>&lt;conclusion&gt;</c>.
  </p>


</paragraphs>
